<title>UK: Trinity Intl sells Canadian operations.</title>
<headline>Trinity Intl sells Canadian operations.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>British newspaper group Trinity International Holdings Plc said on Thursday it sold its Canadian unit to Black Press Ltd for a total of C$58.0 million cash.</p>
<p>The unit, Trinity (NA) Holdings Inc, principally publishes, prints and distributes community newspapers in British Columbia and Alberta.</p>
<p>It had a pre-tax profit of C$6.1 million in 1995 on net assets of C$30.4 million.</p>
<p>The proceeds of the sale will be used to reduce debt.</p>
<p>As a result of the disposal, Trinity will no longer have operations in Canada, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
